// The list of port ranges or `host:port-range` pairs that may be in use for playing SRT or accepting SRT publications
// (depending on the `mode` parameter).
// When playing from or publishing to one of the ports from the range using `srt://server:port` URL with `stream_id` not specified,
// Media Server requests the stream name from `config_external` backend using
// [GET /srt_port_resolve/{port}](https://flussonic.com/doc/api/config-external/#tag/srt/operation/srt_port_resolve) endpoint
// and uses the stream with such name for further playback or publishing.
// So for resolving a stream name by SRT port you need:
// * `srt` ranges set (this option)
// * `config_external` option set in Media Server
// * `/streams` and `/srt_port_resolve` endpoints implemented on the config backend side
// * a stream name in the provisioned external config equals to the name returned by `/srt_port_resolve` for the specified port.
// Note that you should use `stream.srt_publish` and `stream.srt_play` options
// for SRT-specific settings of streams involved to `/srt_port_resolve` logics.
